.TH AVR\-VM\-METRICS 1 "" "avr 0.7.0" "Avrea CLI"
.SH NAME
avr-vm-metrics \- Show CPU/memory/IO metrics for a VM's current or last run.
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B avr vm metrics
[OPTIONS] VM_ID_OR_NAME
.SH DESCRIPTION
Show CPU/memory/IO metrics for a VM's current or last run.
.PP
.SH ARGUMENTS
.TP
\fIVM_ID\fR
\&
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
\fB\-\-org\fR \fITEXT\fR
Organization ID or slug.
.TP
\fB\-\-source\fR \fICHOICE\fR
Metric source. Repeatable; defaults to cpu and memory. (choices: cpu, memory, filesystem, load, disk-io, disk-ops, network; repeatable)
.TP
\fB\-\-start\fR \fIINTEGER\fR
Start time in Unix seconds (single-shot only).
.TP
\fB\-\-end\fR \fIINTEGER\fR
End time in Unix seconds (single-shot only).
.TP
\fB\-\-watch\fR, \fB\-w\fR
Stream live metrics until the run completes; Ctrl-C to exit.
.TP
\fB\-\-json\fR
Emit metrics JSON; watch emits one snapshot per line.
